task: actor-ask-timer (arm the timer only when the reply is not already there; a single-slot Reply; measured on actorAsk)
agent: okay-42
started: 2026-09-06
branch: feature/actor-ask-timer

why: BACKLOG `actor-ask-timer`: every ask arms a timer through
  Async.race(box.receive, Async.sleep(within)) whether the answer takes a
  microsecond or never comes, and Reply is a Channel[R](2) for one
  value. The timer-executor lane already took -20.7% bytes/ask; what is
  left is the shape. Two cheap variants, each measured against the
  current actorAsk under JMH -prof gc: (1) after the send, take the
  reply synchronously if it is already in the box and race only
  otherwise; (2) Reply as a single-slot box instead of a channel. Laws:
  the actor suites, the ask-timeout law, one reply per ask.
